<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agiad dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Agiads</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Agiads were the senior of the two royal houses of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, which was always ruled by two kings at once. They traced their line to Agis I, son of Eurysthenes, and through him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heracles">Heracles</a>. Among the Agiad kings were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleomenes-i">Cleomenes I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonidas-i">Leonidas I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleombrotus-i">Cleombrotus I</a> and the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleomenes-iii">Cleomenes III</a>, and the line died out in the late third century BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agiad-dynasty.jpg" alt="Agiad dynasty" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Di (they-them) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sparta_shield.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
